1
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:05,399
Hey, don't you think we're a bit far out?

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,699
No point in searching
if we're not spread out.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,489
Why did I get stuck with you?

4
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:15,829
Wait, Marlo... You just wanted
alone time with me, didn't you?

5
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:20,169
Hitch... I'm sorry, but you're
not my first choice either.

6
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:23,419
Oh, is that right? Well, good for you.

7
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,089
But, don't you think it's odd?

8
00:00:26,090 --> 00:00:30,139
Why would the Scouts kill
a civilian and run for the hills?

9
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:31,883
They're the same group
that's always risking

10
00:00:31,908 --> 00:00:35,979
their lives for the
sake of humanity.

11
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:39,439
I can't believe you... Did you forget?

12
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,269
Remember what they did
to Stohess District?

13
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:45,149
How they turned it into a battlefield?

14
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:48,410
All those corpses we had to carry?

15
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:52,030
And how Annie's still missing?

16
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:57,919
All of her junk is still in
my room... and it's annoying.

17
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:03,959
But they also uncovered that Titan in
hiding and somehow managed to capture it.

18
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:07,549
You think any other
regiment could do that?

19
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:11,259
If the Scouts get disbanded
like this, humanity can't...

20
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:12,430
Quiet.

21
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:15,270
I hear water.

22
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:20,520
Don't move!

23
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:25,190
Slowly turn this way.

24
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:30,490
You must be a scout.

25
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:35,449
Just like that... Not a word.

26
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:38,160
Now listen to me and do as I...

27
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:44,590
That's right... Hand over your
guns to the one in front.

28
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,800
And not a word, right?

29
00:03:22,770 --> 00:03:27,770
"Trust"

30
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:31,440
"Capital Mitras"

31
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:42,250
Sorry to keep you waiting, Erwin.

32
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:47,880
I know it's sudden, but let's get
the interrogation over with.

33
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:56,509
So, it's unmistakable that the Scout
Regiment murdered a civilian?

34
00:03:56,510 --> 00:03:58,799
Judging by the evidence, at least.

35
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:03,139
Having said that, we can't say
for sure at the time being.

36
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:06,559
Are you saying the Interior Police are
responsible for issuing the search...?

37
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,609
Hey, Peaure!

38
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:13,189
Sorry about him, Commander Dawk.
He's still a rookie, through and through.

39
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:16,529
He doesn't know how we
do things within the walls.

40
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:20,699
Don't you worry about the Interior Police.
We won't write anything about 'em.

41
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:23,869
That goes for their new ODM gear, too.

42
00:04:23,870 --> 00:04:26,080
I appreciate it, Roy.

43
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:30,289
Their new ODM gear...

44
00:04:30,290 --> 00:04:35,049
That buckshot is useless against Titans,
but it's perfect for killing people.

45
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:38,639
It's a weapon practically made
for killing the Scouts...

46
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:42,719
Plus, its existence being hidden
even from us means...

47
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,764
...sooner or later, we might
find ourselves staring down

48
00:04:45,789 --> 00:04:48,849
their muzzles all the same.

49
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:53,650
Anyways, we should hear a report
from them soon, so be patient.

50
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:59,320
Wait up, you fat-ass!

51
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:09,710
You idiot! That way's a dead end!

52
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,040
Shit!

53
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,849
Shit, he's gone!

54
00:05:22,850 --> 00:05:25,019
Find him! Find him!

55
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:26,520
Don't let 'em escape!

56
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:34,779
You're the son of Boss Reeves, right?

57
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:36,110
What's your name?

58
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,449
Flegel.

59
00:05:39,450 --> 00:05:41,239
Nice to meet you, Flegel.

60
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:43,159
I'm Hange Zoe.

61
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:46,579
The thing is, if the Military
Police is after you,

62
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:50,249
that must mean you know the truth
about your father's death, right?

63
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:52,590
Can you tell me what happened?

64
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:59,430
While I was busy taking a piss,
the Interior Police got my old man.

65
00:06:00,550 --> 00:06:05,889
A tall guy wearing a black coat...
he killed my father.

66
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:08,599
In any case, it's great
that you're still alive.

67
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,599
Now we can make the truth public.

68
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:14,149
How's that?! Haven't you seen the paper?!

69
00:06:14,150 --> 00:06:17,319
If the Military Police say the
Scouts did it, that's the truth!

70
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:20,069
My testimony means jack shit!

71
00:06:20,070 --> 00:06:24,989
They know I was there... The Interior
Police found out I saw everything...

72
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:27,949
Now there's nowhere safe for me to go.

73
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:31,749
All I can do is run and hide
in these cramped walls...

74
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:35,879
My life is... shit!

75
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:38,379
Well, you have a point...

76
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:42,180
The thing is, that doesn't
sound like living to me.

77
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:46,099
Look at it this way, Flegel.

78
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:50,269
Instead of scampering around like
a scared little mouse your whole life,

79
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:54,019
wouldn't you rather face up to your enemy,
even if it means risking your life...?

80
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:56,069
Like hell I would!

81
00:06:56,070 --> 00:06:59,689
Not everyone has the same disregard
for their lives as you do!

82
00:06:59,690 --> 00:07:03,279
Not only that, but you have
no right to criticize me either!

83
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:06,829
Don't you care about telling your
company and family the truth?!

84
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:09,079
Huh?! That's just what's best for you!

85
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,869
Of course it is!

86
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:13,459
You oughta start thinking
what's best for you, too!

87
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:16,289
Who's that?! Who's making
a scene on my roof?!

88
00:07:16,290 --> 00:07:18,669
Now then, you're coming with me, Flegel.

89
00:07:18,670 --> 00:07:22,219
Hell no! Your gang already lost!

90
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:24,299
You've been defeated!

91
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,009
What are you talking about?

92
00:07:26,010 --> 00:07:29,560
Defeat is all the Scout
Regiment has ever known!

93
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:34,729
Disguise as Military Police
to get by the guards...

94
00:07:34,730 --> 00:07:38,519
Then figure out where Eren
was taken by snooping around.

95
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,689
To think we'd have no better option...

96
00:07:41,690 --> 00:07:46,659
We just don't have time...
We've got no choice but to do or die.

97
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,780
Captain.

98
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,789
Now then...

99
00:07:50,790 --> 00:07:53,499
Stohess District Military Police.

100
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:56,209
Private Marlo Freudenberg.

101
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:59,039
Captain Levi! It's really him!

102
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:02,379
Same assignment, Private Hitch Dreyse.

103
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,470
As for how we'll dispose of you...

104
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:11,219
Because of you guys, over 100 people
from Stohess District were killed!

105
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,349
Huh?

106
00:08:12,350 --> 00:08:13,180
Hey!

107
00:08:13,181 --> 00:08:17,689
You people... You might think
that you're all heroes of justice,

108
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:21,899
but the victims and their families
were dropped straight into hell!

109
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,110
Yeah, I know.

110
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:30,079
You there... You're from the
Southern Cadet Corps, yeah?

111
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,619
Just like Annie Leonhart.

112
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:35,329
Were you friends of hers?

113
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:41,299
No... I doubt she had any friends.
Being as gloomy and aloof as she was.

114
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:44,920
It's like she was a kid
afraid of other people...

115
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:49,349
I never got the chance to
know anything about her.

116
00:08:49,350 --> 00:08:52,469
And the reason they still
haven't found her...

117
00:08:52,470 --> 00:08:56,309
...is because she was pulverized
by a Titan into a puddle of jelly!

118
00:08:56,310 --> 00:08:57,769
No...

119
00:08:57,770 --> 00:09:02,650
Because the Titan in hiding was...
Annie Leonhart herself.

120
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:07,149
Goddammit, it makes me sick.

121
00:09:07,150 --> 00:09:12,119
Nobody knows a damn thing about
this world... Not us or anyone else.

122
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:16,289
Except for those bastards
at the center of it all.

123
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:20,500
We'll release you both
as soon as we get out of here.

124
00:09:23,090 --> 00:09:25,129
Annie was...

125
00:09:25,130 --> 00:09:28,879
Captain Levi! Please let me help you!

126
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:32,099
I don't think what you
guys are doing is wrong!

127
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:37,769
If I can help correct this world's
injustice, I'll do whatever it takes!

128
00:09:37,770 --> 00:09:40,100
What's with this guy?

129
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,319
I beg of you, Captain Levi!

130
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,569
Not a chance.

131
00:09:44,570 --> 00:09:49,319
I can't tell how prepared you are about
making an enemy of the government.

132
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,739
Let's go.

133
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:53,739
Sasha. Tie them up somewhere nearby.

134
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:54,740
Yes, sir!

135
00:09:58,040 --> 00:09:59,170
Captain.

136
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:02,380
Please let me do it.

137
00:10:06,260 --> 00:10:07,720
Knock yourself out.

138
00:10:15,810 --> 00:10:17,020
Stop.

139
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:23,109
We'll forget what we saw here.

140
00:10:23,110 --> 00:10:26,939
Yeah, you will! Because both
of you will die here!

141
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:28,239
That's not what he said!

142
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,989
Letting you two run free is too dangerous.

143
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:33,489
I'll take it upon myself to kill you!

144
00:10:33,490 --> 00:10:35,079
Please, believe us!

145
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:38,789
We know you guys are fighting
to try and save humanity!

146
00:10:38,790 --> 00:10:39,750
Right, Hitch?!

147
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:40,580
Mmm, mmm!

148
00:10:40,581 --> 00:10:45,379
As if I could trust you.
Especially you, Mr. Bowl Cut.

149
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:48,299
Who in their right mind
would cut their hair like that?

150
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:51,220
You'll get no sympathy from this guy!

151
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:57,220
Hitch, run!

152
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:02,059
My gun is faster, you know.

153
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:04,189
Wanna take your chances?

154
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:07,319
Your knife and my gun... Let's race!

155
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:09,899
Wait! I'm really your ally!

156
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:13,109
Why the hell would anyone
believe you'd wanna join us?

157
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:18,120
We're so severely outmatched,
you really think we can save humanity?

158
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:21,909
Then, why are you...?

159
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:25,040
Why are you still with the Scouts then?

160
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:30,339
I picked the wrong regiment to join.

161
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:34,679
As long as you guys have it in you
to risk your lives and keep fighting...

162
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:36,640
...I will trust you.

163
00:11:42,270 --> 00:11:44,189
Hitch!

164
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:45,559
You damn horse face!

165
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:49,689
Wait, Hitch! He was just testing us!

166
00:11:49,690 --> 00:11:51,280
Huh?!

167
00:11:53,070 --> 00:11:54,949
Hey, you.

168
00:11:54,950 --> 00:11:59,699
What would you have done
if I swung the knife at you?

169
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:02,250
Why did you trust me so much?

170
00:12:03,370 --> 00:12:07,329
Somehow or another,
you remind me of a guy that I hate.

171
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:09,000
A damn idiot.

172
00:12:10,210 --> 00:12:14,380
This idiot... Is it the same
one Annie talked about?

173
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:17,759
Hell if I know.

174
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:19,510
Everyone's an idiot.

175
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:27,349
Fortunately, we're both just as dumb.

176
00:12:27,350 --> 00:12:30,940
Marlo, I think you proved your dedication.

177
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:35,949
That should be enough
to convince Captain Levi.

178
00:12:35,950 --> 00:12:38,280
We're counting on you.

179
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:45,459
That over there is the least
manned checkpoint around.

180
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:48,459
All right. We'll handle it ourselves.

181
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:51,499
Get back to your squad
before it's suspicious.

182
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,710
Yes, sir.

183
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:56,300
Marlo, Hitch.

184
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,050
We're grateful.

185
00:13:00,510 --> 00:13:02,429
Sir!

186
00:13:02,430 --> 00:13:03,719
Let's go!

187
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:05,940
It's our turn to pick a fight!

188
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:11,190
Hmm?

189
00:13:30,330 --> 00:13:31,540
It's me.

190
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:36,589
Captain, he's...

191
00:13:36,590 --> 00:13:38,719
With the Interior Police.

192
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:41,679
I've got a few questions for him.

193
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:42,970
Let's move.

194
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:07,459
How dumb can you be?
Running into a deserted dump like this...

195
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:09,539
Shit!

196
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:13,169
But I owe you one, Flegel Reeves.

197
00:14:13,170 --> 00:14:17,549
When you got away and
gave us the slip, I really...

198
00:14:17,550 --> 00:14:22,010
I thought I was screwed!

199
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:30,730
For a minute there, I
thought they'd kill me.

200
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:35,519
Nice knowing you, Flegel. Thanks a bunch!

201
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,279
Ah, wait!

202
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:39,149
Why was my old man killed?!

203
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,989
Did the Interior Police do it?!

204
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:43,699
Huh? What does it matter to you?

205
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:47,199
You're about to be fresh corpse.

206
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,789
I-I wanna know before I die!

207
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:52,499
What did he ever do to
deserve being killed?!

208
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,749
Eh? You don't know?

209
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:59,469
He betrayed us and sided
with those damn Scouts.

210
00:14:59,470 --> 00:15:00,759
Betrayed?

211
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:05,099
So you're saying it was the Interior
Police that made him kidnap those Scouts?!

212
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:07,929
Except it was a different squad than us.

213
00:15:07,930 --> 00:15:10,769
Guess he didn't say a damn thing.

214
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:13,939
Not to his dimwit son.

215
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:16,569
And what if he would've refused?

216
00:15:16,570 --> 00:15:21,739
Well, he'd have known a bit too much,
so he would've had to die.

217
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:23,699
What a fool.

218
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:27,410
Look where caring for the city
and workers got 'em.

219
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:32,409
You would never understand.

220
00:15:32,410 --> 00:15:33,619
Hmm?

221
00:15:33,620 --> 00:15:36,749
Talking like you're smart shit...

222
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:39,379
My old man taught me something.

223
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:42,839
That merchants gotta follow their nose.

224
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:45,179
And I'm damn glad that I did.

225
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:48,219
Because I found the people
who could avenge my old man!

226
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,719
And I side with them!

227
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:53,809
What's the matter, Flegel? Go on and
oink like a pig to be slaughtered!

228
00:15:53,810 --> 00:15:56,559
You had your time, but it's over!

229
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:58,770
Look above you, morons!

230
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:13,909
Ouch!

231
00:16:13,910 --> 00:16:16,459
Section Commander! You're too wild!

232
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:20,089
Hell yeah! Did you hear that, everyone?!

233
00:16:20,090 --> 00:16:25,090
The... Scout Regiment...? Why?

234
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:30,469
Not so deserted, eh?

235
00:16:30,470 --> 00:16:32,769
Perhaps it looks that way to you.

236
00:16:32,770 --> 00:16:34,189
But, sorry.

237
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:38,309
I know it doesn't look like much,
but we still live here.

238
00:16:38,310 --> 00:16:40,069
We heard everything.

239
00:16:40,070 --> 00:16:45,359
The Interior Police and their schemes...
Everyone here is a witness.

240
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,949
S-So, what does it matter?

241
00:16:47,950 --> 00:16:50,989
It's the government that
decides what's the truth!

242
00:16:50,990 --> 00:16:55,039
You fools... Don't think you can
do this and get away with it!

243
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:57,669
You're all in for a world of hu...

244
00:16:57,670 --> 00:17:00,749
Everyone... Don't worry.

245
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:03,709
The Reeves Company will protect this city.

246
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:06,429
As of today, I, Flegel Reeves...

247
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:08,180
I'm the boss.

248
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:16,390
So... from now... you can count... on me.

249
00:17:20,650 --> 00:17:22,689
We're counting on you, Boss.

250
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:24,689
Speak up, man!

251
00:17:24,690 --> 00:17:26,569
Congrats on the job.

252
00:17:26,570 --> 00:17:29,529
Keep an eye on these Interior Police.

253
00:17:29,530 --> 00:17:30,780
Right.

254
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,330
Stop it...

255
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,750
Where are Eren and Christa?

256
00:17:45,170 --> 00:17:46,799
Oh, you're so brave.

257
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:48,923
That checkpoint back
there was just recruits

258
00:17:48,948 --> 00:17:51,599
who could barely
wipe their own ass.

259
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:55,849
You think you're some sort of hero,
beating them down?

260
00:17:55,850 --> 00:17:58,640
What an atrocious thing we've done.

261
00:18:01,150 --> 00:18:04,529
But what's more atrocious
is this mouth of yours.

262
00:18:04,530 --> 00:18:08,859
I recommend you start talking
while you're still able to use it.

263
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:11,320
Where are Eren and Christa?

264
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:16,409
It's no use!

265
00:18:16,410 --> 00:18:18,409
All that's left for you now is

266
00:18:18,434 --> 00:18:22,919
to run and hide inside these
walls, covered in mud and shit!

267
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:28,009
If you don't turn yourselves in, every
last Scout we captured will get the noose!

268
00:18:28,010 --> 00:18:32,390
Starting with the one most
guilty of all, Erwin Smith!

269
00:18:35,510 --> 00:18:37,059
Shut up.

270
00:18:37,060 --> 00:18:40,189
That's for not answering my question.

271
00:18:40,190 --> 00:18:43,519
Some Scouts' lives are
more valuable than others.

272
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:47,779
Only those dumb enough
to acknowledge that join us.

273
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:50,199
Tell me where Eren and Christa are at.

274
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,949
I-I don't know!

275
00:18:51,950 --> 00:18:53,989
I'm not allowed to know!

276
00:18:53,990 --> 00:18:56,909
Kenny Ackermann is a very cautious man!

277
00:18:56,910 --> 00:18:58,999
Ackermann?

278
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,959
I know Kenny... Is that his last name?

279
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,710
It is, but...

280
00:19:05,250 --> 00:19:10,719
True, there's a lot of things he doesn't
divulge... Especially the important stuff.

281
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:13,089
But you must have a rough idea.

282
00:19:13,090 --> 00:19:15,179
You best try to remember.

283
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:15,760
...Stop it!

284
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:16,430
...You still have plenty of bones
left to break. ...Stop it!

285
00:19:16,431 --> 00:19:19,679
...You still have plenty
of bones left to break.

286
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:23,149
You... You're insane!

287
00:19:23,150 --> 00:19:24,859
Maybe I am.

288
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:26,650
Someone's coming from that way!

289
00:19:29,190 --> 00:19:30,610
More than one!

290
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:34,489
Told you so, Captain.

291
00:19:34,490 --> 00:19:37,029
It's no use.

292
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:42,160
One way or another, the Scouts
will soon come to an end!

293
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:52,379
I've seen you in better shape.

294
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:56,220
And to think you were
lecturing me the other day.

295
00:20:00,310 --> 00:20:02,389
You're getting an audience with the King.

296
00:20:02,390 --> 00:20:07,569
They'll decide how to dismantle the Scouts
and announce your final sentence.

297
00:20:07,570 --> 00:20:09,320
Nile, huh?

298
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:13,569
Where was your house?

299
00:20:13,570 --> 00:20:15,660
Stohess District, was it?

300
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:23,290
Is Marie...? Is your family doing well?

301
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:29,339
They're doing fine. Both
Marie and the kids.

302
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:32,259
I haven't been home in a while, but...

303
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:35,050
...it's around Eastern Wall Rose.

304
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:37,890
I see...

305
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:42,140
What's with the odd questions?

306
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:47,099
I entrusted something to Commander Pyxis.

307
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:49,940
When, and if the time comes...

308
00:20:51,570 --> 00:20:54,699
When it comes, I will only watch.

309
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:59,410
It's up to you to decide. You... and them.

310
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:08,539
So, I take it not much
came out of Erwin in the end.

311
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:13,259
Indeed... He must not have learned
any secrets from Pastor Nick.

312
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:17,006
Historia Reiss can make all the
claims she wants about her name,

313
00:21:17,031 --> 00:21:19,049
but they'll amount to nothing.

314
00:21:19,050 --> 00:21:20,349
How silly.

315
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:24,599
In any case, they're all nothing
more than birds in a cage.

316
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,770
Just waiting to die...

317
00:21:28,650 --> 00:21:30,019
Excuse me.

318
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:32,569
Erwin Smith has arrived.

319
00:21:32,570 --> 00:21:35,989
Very well. We're coming.

320
00:21:35,990 --> 00:21:41,079
Once we finally execute him,
all will be according to plan.

321
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:45,079
And just like they always have,
the wall's secrets will stay safe.

322
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:47,830
We'll protect the peace within the walls.

323
00:21:49,330 --> 00:21:51,040
Forever...

324
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:00,799
Erwin.

325
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:03,890
Do you have any last words?

326
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:42,989
In order to protect the kingdom...

327
00:23:42,990 --> 00:23:47,659
In order to protect the King,
they kept the truth hidden.

328
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:52,489
However, in doing so, they invite
an uprising of the people.

329
00:23:52,490 --> 00:23:54,039
Next Episode: "Reply."

330
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:56,340
"Reply"
